1. Physical Layer (Layer 1)
What does it do?

This layer is responsible for sending raw bits (0s and 1s) through cables or wireless signals.

It doesn't understand websites, emails, or files.

It only sends electrical, light, or radio signals.

Devices
Ethernet Cable
Fiber Cable
Hub
Repeater
Example

When you plug an Ethernet cable into your laptop, you're using the Physical Layer.
